comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-08T14:06:01.280Z","harness:codex","GitHub source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/937. Duplicate check searched all statuses for alias-indexed package rows, duplicated packages, catalog totals, and package-list count semantics. Closed pm-59gj and pm-x6jf own the package/SDK foundations but not this projection defect; no canonical issue existed."
  "2026-08-08T16:46:59.893Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence (2026-08-08): full release pipeline reached the pre-commit hosted-review boundary after all local gates passed. Exact coverage: 460 files, 7072 tests, statements 50283/50283, branches 36738/36738, functions 10330/10330, lines 48684/48684. Static quality/docstrings, docs/skills, SDK surface, package boundary/parity, token/context/retrieval/tracker/security/version, packed npx (13 packages), and 88-command temporary package-first dogfood all passed. Manual packed external acceptance also passed all-status duplicates, 13 unique package rows with aliases, SDK direction-independent merge, package-manage output resolution, merge install, and health classification. The remaining greptile gate refusal is expected before a reviewable commit: no committed code changes to review against main."
  "2026-08-08T17:06:12.038Z","harness:codex","Review feedback: DeepScan defect 231762204 validly identified that the integration test cast result.json.details.packages without an explicit runtime guard. Reopened and claimed the canonical package-cardinality item to add fail-closed array validation before use."
  "2026-08-08T17:09:34.246Z","harness:codex","Review fix evidence: DeepScan NULL_POINTER 231762204 addressed by defaulting the optional JSON package collection to an empty array and asserting non-empty before cardinality access. Focused integration test and the full repo lint/static/token/context/tracker/SDK gates passed."
  "2026-08-08T17:27:21.676Z","harness:codex","Review feedback: CodeRabbit found the package-list dogfood mock still reports total 10 while the grouped catalog fixture contains nine packages. Reopened the canonical GH-937 item to derive the count from the shared fixture."
  "2026-08-08T17:41:04.388Z","harness:codex","Review fix evidence: package catalog and compatibility-list totals now derive from the same package-row fixture, preventing cardinality drift. Linked integration/dogfood tests pass; full suite is exact 100/100/100/100."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-08T16:49:50.252Z","harness:codex","Catalog cardinality should describe installable packages, while aliases remain resolution metadata; duplicating rows per alias corrupts package counts and agent context."
